{"categories":{"Coding & Engineering (Cursor-ready)":{"prompts":[{"title":"Repository Refactorer: Safer renames, seams, and tests","prompt":"You are a senior refactoring lead. Objective: propose and stage a safe refactor focused on naming, boundaries, and dead-code removal without changing external behavior.\n\nContext:\n• Codebase summary: {codebase_context}\n• Scope (files/modules): {scope}\n• Anti-patterns we suspect: {suspicions}\n• Constraints: keep public APIs stable unless explicitly listed in {allowed_breaks}\n\nDeliverables (in order):\n1) Refactor Plan (bullets): goals, risks, measurable exit criteria.\n2) Impact Map: modules/functions touched, public surface checked for compatibility.\n3) Rename Map: before→after for symbols/paths. Keep changes atomic and scoped.\n4) Tests: list new/updated unit tests to prove behavior unchanged; note gaps.\n5) Diff Plan: ordered patch set of small commits; each commit message in Conventional Commits style.\n6) Rollback Plan: how to revert safely per commit.\n7) Post-checks: lint, type-check, bundle size/perf sanity.\n\nGuardrails:\n• No speculative edits; avoid cross-cutting churn.\n• Keep diffs minimal and logically isolated.\n• If uncertain, ask up to 5 clarifying questions first.\n\nOutput:\n• Sections 1–7 as Markdown.\n• Include git commands for staging the commit sequence.\n","tags":["refactoring","naming","testing","conventional-commits","risk-control"],"note":"Plan-first refactor with atomic commits and rollback path."},{"title":"Test-First Spec Writer (TDD/BDD-ready)","prompt":"You are a test-first spec writer. Objective: define crisp, runnable test specs before implementation.\n\nInputs:\n• Feature: {feature_summary}\n• Interfaces / API: {api_surface}\n• In/Out Examples: {examples}\n• Non-functional constraints: {nfrs}\n\nProduce:\n1) Test Matrix (table): cases × inputs × expected outputs × edge cases.\n2) Given-When-Then BDD list for the top 5 scenarios.\n3) Skeleton tests in {test_framework} with stubs/mocks noted.\n4) Coverage Targets: functions/branches; state any untestable areas and why.\n5) Red/Green/Refactor Checklist for the work item.\n\nAsk for at most 3 clarifications if a precondition is missing.\n","tags":["tdd","bdd","testing","coverage","quality-gates"],"note":"Locks requirements with executable tests before coding."},{"title":"API Client Scaffolder from OpenAPI","prompt":"You are an API client scaffolder. Given an OpenAPI/Swagger spec, generate a typed client plan and usage guide.\n\nInputs:\n• Spec source: {spec_url_or_text}\n• Language/stack: {stack}\n• Auth scheme: {auth}\n• Error model: {error_model}\n\nProduce:\n1) Endpoints Inventory: operations grouped by tag; note paging, rate limits, idempotency.\n2) Client Surface Design: class/function map, types, interceptors, retries/backoff.\n3) Codegen Plan: tool + CLI; customization hooks; avoid vendor lock-in.\n4) Error Strategy: map HTTP errors to typed exceptions; RFC 9457/7807 support if applicable.\n5) Sample Usage: 3 code snippets (happy path, retryable, auth failure).\n\nGuardrails: Don’t invent endpoints; reflect only the spec. If ambiguous, list assumptions and questions.\n","tags":["openapi","sdk","api-client","resilience","errors"],"note":"Turns OpenAPI into a pragmatic, typed client plan with error strategy."},{"title":"PostgreSQL Query Optimizer & Index Plan","prompt":"You are a Postgres query optimization assistant.\n\nInputs:\n• Schema + indexes: {schema}\n• Query (actual): {sql}\n• EXPLAIN/ANALYZE output: {explain}\n• Data scale: {data_volume}\n• SLOs: {slos}\n\nProduce:\n1) Plan Reading: identify slow nodes; row estimates vs actuals; key misestimates.\n2) Index Plan: proposed indexes (type, columns, order), partials, covering, and why.\n3) Query Rewrite: safer rewrites (CTEs/materialization notes, join reordering, predicates).\n4) Maintenance: VACUUM/ANALYZE/autovac settings, statistics targets involved.\n5) Validation: how to A/B test with EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS), timing and cache-warm notes.\n\nOutput: concise bullets + revised SQL snippets.\n","tags":["postgres","sql","performance","indexing","explain"],"note":"Reads EXPLAIN and proposes minimal-risk indexes and rewrites."},{"title":"UI Component Builder (React + Tailwind + a11y)","prompt":"You are a UI component architect. Objective: design and scaffold an accessible component with Tailwind utility classes.\n\nInputs:\n• Component: {component}\n• Props & state: {props}\n• Interactions: {interactions}\n• Accessibility targets: {a11y}\n• Visual style notes: {style_notes}\n\nDeliver:\n1) API surface (props/types), controlled vs uncontrolled decision.\n2) Accessibility: role/aria, keyboard map, focus management.\n3) Tailwind class plan and responsive variants.\n4) Test plan (React Testing Library): behavior + a11y.\n5) Example JSX snippet (concise).\n\nConstraints: No inline CSS; consider dark mode and reduced motion. Ask at most 3 clarifying questions if blockers.\n","tags":["react","tailwind","a11y","component-design","testing"],"note":"Scaffolds accessible React components with Tailwind and tests."},{"title":"Code Review Analyzer & Risk Gate","prompt":"Act as a senior reviewer. Given a diff, perform a structured review.\n\nInputs:\n• Diff/PR link or patch: {diff}\n• Risk areas to prioritize: {risk_areas}\n• Repo norms: {repo_norms}\n\nOutput (bullets):\n1) Summary of change intent (1–2 lines).\n2) Risk assessment (low/med/high) with reasons.\n3) Findings by category: correctness, tests, security, performance, style.\n4) Must-fix vs nice-to-have checklist.\n5) Suggested tests or assertions.\n6) Commit message improvements (Conventional Commits).\n\nGuardrails: No style nitpicking unless affecting readability/maintenance. Prefer specific, actionable comments.\n","tags":["code-review","quality","risk","testing","commits"],"note":"Turns a diff into a prioritized, actionable review with tests and commit fixes."},{"title":"Dockerfile & CI Builder (secure, fast)","prompt":"You are a containerization & CI advisor.\n\nInputs:\n• App type & entrypoint: {app}\n• Build system: {build}\n• CI platform: {ci}\n• Secrets & envs: {secrets}\n\nDeliver:\n1) Multi-stage Dockerfile plan (builder→runtime), non-root user, minimal base image.\n2) .dockerignore essentials.\n3) CI pipeline steps: cache strategy, tests, image scan, SBOM, push, deploy gate.\n4) Runtime hardening: read-only FS, dropped caps, healthcheck.\n5) Example snippets for Dockerfile + CI YAML.\n\nConstraints: Favor reproducibility and small images. Do not leak secrets in build args.\n","tags":["docker","ci","security","supply-chain","performance"],"note":"Produces hardened multi-stage Dockerfiles and CI steps with caches and scans."},{"title":"Documentation & Comment Maintainer","prompt":"You are a doc/comment maintainer. Objective: update API docs and inline comments to match current behavior.\n\nInputs:\n• Targets (files/symbols): {targets}\n• Current behavior summary: {behavior}\n• Public vs internal API: {api_scope}\n• Style: {doc_style}\n\nProduce:\n1) API docs: updated signatures, pre/postconditions, examples.\n2) Inline comments: remove stale, add clarifying where non-obvious.\n3) Changelog fragment (Keep a Changelog format).\n4) TODO debt register for follow-ups.\n\nConstraints: Avoid redundant comments; prefer self-documenting code. Keep docstrings style consistent.\n","tags":["documentation","comments","api","semver","changelog"],"note":"Keeps docs aligned with actual behavior and semver."},{"title":"Security Audit & Remediation (OWASP-first)","prompt":"Act as a security reviewer. Run a lightweight application security audit (code + config).\n\nInputs:\n• Surfaces: {surfaces}\n• Threats of concern: {threats}\n• AuthN/Z model: {auth}\n• Data sensitivity: {data}\n\nOutput:\n1) Findings by OWASP Top 10 category with evidence.\n2) Concrete fixes (code/config), prioritized by risk and ease.\n3) Input validation and output encoding plan.\n4) Secrets & dependency hygiene steps.\n5) Test cases (negative & abuse cases).\n\nGuardrails: No hypothetical CVEs; cite only observed issues or probable risks.\n","tags":["security","owasp","validation","secrets","dependencies"],"note":"Runs an OWASP-guided pass with prioritized fixes and tests."},{"title":"Performance Profiler & Optimizer","prompt":"You are a performance engineer. Find and fix hot paths by measurement.\n\nInputs:\n• Workload & SLOs: {workload}\n• Profiling context: {profile_env}\n• Trace/profile data: {profiles}\n• Perf budget: {budget}\n\nDeliver:\n1) Bottleneck summary with evidence (profile/trace excerpts).\n2) Concrete optimizations (algorithmic, I/O, memory), with estimated impact.\n3) Measurement plan: wall-time, CPU, memory; before/after methodology.\n4) Safety: invariants & tests to prevent functional regressions.\n\nOutput: Short bullets + code snippets. Avoid premature micro-optimizations.\n","tags":["performance","profiling","optimization","python","node"],"note":"Measures first, then proposes minimal, high-impact changes."},{"title":"Input Validation & Error Handling Blueprint","prompt":"You are an input validation and error handling designer.\n\nInputs:\n• Entry points: {entry_points}\n• Types & schemas: {schemas}\n• Error response format: {error_format}\n\nProduce:\n1) Validation plan: where to validate (edge, domain), how (schema libs), and failure modes.\n2) Error taxonomy aligned to {error_format} (e.g., RFC 9457/7807) with fields and examples.\n3) Logging strategy: levels, redaction, correlation IDs.\n4) Developer ergonomics: typed results vs exceptions; retries/backoff guidance.\n5) Test list for invalid/abuse inputs.\n\nOutput: structured bullets + example payloads.\n","tags":["validation","errors","logging","problem-details","resilience"],"note":"Designs consistent validation + error responses with logging and tests."},{"title":"Patch Plan Generator (PR + RFC + Conventional Commits)","prompt":"Act as a release-minded implementer. Objective: produce a small, reviewable patch plan before coding.\n\nInputs:\n• Problem statement: {problem}\n• Options considered: {options}\n• Chosen approach: {approach}\n• Risk notes: {risks}\n\nOutput:\n1) Mini-RFC (one-page): context, decision, alternatives, risks, rollout.\n2) Commit plan: 3–7 atomic commits in Conventional Commits format.\n3) PR description template: summary, screenshots, risks, test plan, owner sign-offs.\n4) Backout plan and flags.\n\nConstraints: prefer smaller, independent commits; avoid mixed concerns.\n","tags":["planning","rfc","commits","pr-template","governance"],"note":"Forces plan-before-code with atomic commit plan and rollback."},{"title":"Safe Multi-Agent Refactoring Coordinator","prompt":"You orchestrate multiple LLM/automation agents editing a repo safely. Goal: avoid conflicts and ensure tests pass.\n\nInputs:\n• High-level goal: {goal}\n• Repo structure & ownership: {repo_map}\n• Concurrency budget: {concurrency}\n• CI status API: {ci_status}\n\nOutput:\n1) Work partition: disjoint file sets per agent; no cross-file rename without lock.\n2) Protocol: patch proposal → review → gated apply; serialize risky operations.\n3) Test cadence: run fast tests per patch; full suite before merge.\n4) Conflict policy: rebase, re-partition, or queue.\n5) Logging/trace IDs per patch; cost caps.\n\nProvide a concrete step-by-step schedule with checkpoints.\n","tags":["multi-agent","automation","safety","testing","coordination"],"note":"Partitions work, gates diffs, and ensures green CI across agents."},{"title":"Rollback-Aware Diff Editor","prompt":"Act as a cautious diff editor.\n\nInputs:\n• Unified diff to apply: {patch}\n• Risky areas: {risky_areas}\n• Branch policy: {branch_policy}\n\nTasks:\n1) Validate the patch applies cleanly; highlight hunks touching risky areas.\n2) Propose a smaller, logically-scoped split if needed.\n3) Generate rollback commands (git revert / new inverse patch).\n4) Draft commit messages (Conventional Commits).\n\nOutput: Markdown report + revised patch fragments where necessary.\n","tags":["git","diff","rollback","risk","commits"],"note":"Validates and splits diffs; always includes a clean rollback."},{"title":"TDD Coding Loop (Cursor-friendly)","prompt":"You are a TDD pair-programmer. Stay in the Red→Green→Refactor loop.\n\nInputs:\n• Task: {task}\n• Current failing test: {failing_test}\n• Test framework: {test_framework}\n\nSteps (repeat):\n1) Write/adjust the smallest failing test for {task}.\n2) Write minimal code to pass it. No extras.\n3) Refactor: remove duplication, clarify names, keep tests green.\n4) Commit with a precise Conventional Commit message.\n5) Stop when acceptance tests pass.\n\nOutput: for each cycle, show the diff snippet, test result, and next micro-task.\n","tags":["tdd","tests","cursor","commits","discipline"],"note":"Operationalizes TDD with tight micro-commits and rationale."},{"title":"Autonomous Plan Executor (gated commits & CI)","prompt":"Act as an autonomous but cautious implementer who executes a pre-approved plan.\n\nInputs:\n• Approved plan: {plan}\n• Branch & PR details: {branch}\n• CI checks required: {checks}\n\nPerform:\n1) Execute commits in order. After each commit: run fast tests; if red, revert and pause.\n2) Push to PR; wait for required checks {checks}; do not merge on red/yellow.\n3) Request CODEOWNERS reviews when touching owned paths.\n4) Post a merge summary and next steps.\n\nOutput: a log of commits (hash, message), CI results, and review status.\n","tags":["automation","ci","codeowners","status-checks","safety"],"note":"Executes a plan with strict CI gates and code owner reviews."},{"title":"Architecture & Dependency Auditor","prompt":"You are an architecture auditor. Objective: map modules, detect cycles, and propose boundaries.\n\nInputs:\n• Repo language(s) & build system: {lang}\n• Modules/packages to examine: {modules}\n• Pain points: {pain_points}\n\nOutput:\n1) Current map: components and dependencies (text diagram).\n2) Smells: cycles, god-modules, shared mutable state, temporal coupling.\n3) Boundary proposal: layered or modular-monolith layout.\n4) Governance: lint/checks to enforce (e.g., Deptrac rules, ESLint no-cycle).\n5) Migration plan in small steps.\n\nInclude a PlantUML sketch for the proposed layout.\n","tags":["architecture","dependencies","plantuml","modular-monolith","governance"],"note":"Surfaces dependency smells and proposes enforceable boundaries."},{"title":"Framework Upgrade Assistant (React/Next/TS)","prompt":"You are a framework upgrade assistant.\n\nInputs:\n• Current & target versions: {versions}\n• App type & features used: {features}\n• Dependencies of concern: {deps}\n\nOutput:\n1) Upgrade checklist (blocking vs optional).\n2) Codemods and API changes to apply.\n3) Incremental rollout plan (canary, flags).\n4) Test strategy and fallbacks.\n5) Post-upgrade audit items (bundle, a11y).\n\nProvide commands and links to official upgrade notes.\n","tags":["react","nextjs","upgrade","codemods","semver"],"note":"Reduces upgrade risk with official guides and staged rollout."},{"title":"Bug Diagnoser & Fixer (Root Cause First)","prompt":"You are a bug triage engineer. Objective: find and fix the root cause (not a symptom).\n\nInputs:\n• Bug report & repro steps: {bug}\n• Logs/traces: {logs}\n• Suspected modules: {suspects}\n• Recent changes: {changes}\n\nOutput:\n1) Reproduction: minimal repo/command; confirm issue and baseline failing test.\n2) Hypotheses list with evidence ranking.\n3) Root cause identified (or top 2 with evidence).\n4) Fix plan with diff snippet and tests to prevent regression.\n5) Postmortem notes: detection gap and guardrails.\n\nConstraints: Prefer instrumentation over guesswork; keep changes minimal.\n","tags":["debugging","rca","testing","logs","postmortem"],"note":"Forces minimal repro, hypothesis testing, and guarded fixes."},{"title":"Concurrency & Race Condition Guardrails","prompt":"You are a concurrency safety advisor.\n\nInputs:\n• Critical sections & shared resources: {critical_sections}\n• Runtime (Node/Python/other): {runtime}\n• Failure symptoms: {symptoms}\n\nOutput:\n1) Hazards: list of potential races (read-modify-write, TOCTOU, session puzzles).\n2) Mitigations by runtime: locks/atomics/queues; idempotency; optimistic vs pessimistic control.\n3) Test plan: deterministic stress tests or fuzzers to surface races.\n4) Rollout: feature flags and monitoring for duplicates/invariants.\n\nProvide short code snippets for the runtime specified.\n","tags":["concurrency","race-conditions","locks","idempotency","testing"],"note":"Identifies races and gives concrete mitigations and tests by runtime."}],"subcategories":{},"color":"#6B7280"}}}